cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite the dataset itself."
type: dataset
title: "MCP Parameter-Description Ablation: Token Savings Without Accuracy Loss"
authors:
  - family-names: Clouâtre
    given-names: Hugues
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4291-1999"
repository-code: "https://github.com/clouatre-labs/param-description-experiments"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >
  Supplementary dataset for a pre-registered, blind-scored ablation study testing
  whether moving parameter-level detail out of an MCP tool's description string and
  into inputSchema.properties[*].description costs parameter-filling accuracy. Across
  two experiments (320 and 160 calls; claude-haiku-4-5 and claude-sonnet-5), the
  pre-registered Mann-Whitney U primary tests found no detectable accuracy difference
  at two scoring resolutions, while input tokens per call dropped significantly for
  the schema-level placement — demonstrating a roughly 45% tool-description token
  saving at no measurable accuracy cost. Includes pre-registered protocols, rubrics,
  raw call transcripts, blind scores, and all harness, scorer, and analysis scripts.
keywords:
  - model-context-protocol
  - mcp
  - llm-evaluation
  - tool-use
  - function-calling
  - ablation-study
  - token-efficiency
  - prompt-engineering
  - input-schema
  - schema-design
  - cost-reduction
  - agentic-ai
